{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["Also to this — for already 'ויחזק לב פרעה' of his own accord, and now too it hardened on its own. But in the frogs it is written: והכבד את לבו — that he himself intended to harden his heart. Therefore in the section of the mixed swarms it says: ויכבד פרעה את לבו גם בפעם הזאת — for he had already hardened his heart on another occasion."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וגם עתה נחזק מאליו' uses a passive/reflexive form; rendered as 'it hardened on its own' to convey Rashbam's contrast with Pharaoh's active/intentional hardening in the case of the frogs."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:43.157107398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}